     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p4-gradient-method-block",
     "replacement": "To calculate gradient:\n\n1. Find the **rise**: the vertical change from the left point to the right point.\n  a. Positive if the line slopes upwards from left to right.\n  b. Negative if the line slopes downwards from left to right.\n2. Find the **run**: the horizontal change from the left point to the right point.\n3. Calculate gradient $m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}$.\n4. Simplify the fraction, if you can.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p4-gradient-method-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "09366c171c3688cf63c771c501f6663e8a7d643b5fecfc0b023826bf253c3db5",
